// ============================================================
// 各Section内容生成
// ============================================================
function getIntroBody(slug, titleEn) {
  const content = {
    'three-phase-vs-single-phase-avr-guide': 'Voltage instability is one of the most common causes of equipment failure in both residential and industrial settings. In Africa, where voltage fluctuations regularly exceed 260V, choosing the right automatic voltage regulator (AVR) can mean the difference between uninterrupted operations and costly downtime. The critical first decision is whether you need a single-phase or three-phase AVR system. This guide breaks down everything you need to make the right choice for your specific application, load requirements, and budget.',
    'avr-for-solar-power-systems': 'Solar power systems are transforming energy generation across Africa and emerging markets, but they introduce unique voltage regulation challenges. Unlike stable grid power, solar installations experience fluctuating DC-to-AC conversion that can produce voltage irregularities dangerous to sensitive electronics. An AVR for solar power systems addresses these challenges by ensuring that the AC output feeding your home or facility remains stable regardless of solar panel performance variations. This guide covers why voltage regulation is essential for solar installations and how to select the right AVR for your setup.',
    'how-to-calculate-avr-kva-requirements': 'Selecting the correct KVA capacity for your AVR is the most important decision in the purchasing process. An undersized AVR will overload and fail to protect your equipment during voltage sags. An oversized AVR represents unnecessary capital expenditure and reduced efficiency at low loads. This guide provides the exact formulas and practical examples used by electrical engineers to properly size AVR systems for residential, commercial, and industrial applications. No guesswork required.',
    'avr-for-industrial-motors-compressors': 'Industrial electric motors and air compressors represent significant capital investments for any manufacturing or processing operation. These devices are particularly vulnerable to voltage fluctuations, with voltage sags causing increased current draw and voltage surges potentially destroying motor windings. The financial impact of motor failure extends far beyond repair costs—it includes production downtime, lost throughput, and potential safety hazards. YOKE AVR systems are specifically designed to protect motor loads with the high inrush current handling capacity required for industrial applications.',
    'signs-your-avr-needs-replacement': 'Automatic voltage regulators are designed for longevity, but like all electrical equipment, they have a finite service life. Recognizing the warning signs of a failing AVR before it completely breaks down can save you thousands of dollars in equipment damage and business interruption. This guide identifies seven critical warning signs that indicate your AVR requires professional inspection or replacement. Early detection is key—learn what to watch for and how to respond.',
    'avr-in-healthcare-medical-equipment': 'Healthcare facilities depend on a continuous, clean power supply to maintain life-saving equipment, diagnostic systems, and patient monitoring devices. Voltage irregularities in hospital environments can have life-threatening consequences. A voltage sag of even a few cycles can restart sensitive equipment, while surges can cause permanent damage to expensive diagnostic hardware. This guide explores why AVR systems are a critical component of healthcare facility power quality management.',
    'understanding-appliance-voltage-tolerance': 'Different electrical appliances are designed to tolerate different ranges of voltage variation. Understanding these tolerances helps you appreciate why voltage regulation is not just a luxury but a necessity for protecting your investment. Most modern appliances are designed for 220-240V nominal systems with a tolerance of approximately ±10%, but African power grids can produce fluctuations far outside these safe limits. This guide provides comprehensive voltage tolerance data for common household and commercial appliances.',
    'avr-for-data-centers-it-equipment': 'Modern data centers and enterprise IT infrastructure represent billions of dollars in capital investment that depends entirely on clean, reliable power. Server equipment, network switches, and storage arrays are extremely sensitive to voltage irregularities. Unlike desktop computers, enterprise hardware operates 24/7, meaning it is constantly exposed to whatever power quality the grid delivers. This guide covers why AVR is the essential first layer of defense in any comprehensive power protection strategy for IT environments.',
    'avr-renewable-energy-systems-guide': 'Renewable energy systems, from rooftop solar to utility-scale wind farms, are characterized by variable power output that creates unique voltage regulation challenges. The very nature of converting variable DC from solar panels or wind turbines into usable AC power introduces frequency and voltage fluctuations that can damage both the renewable system itself and any connected loads. This guide examines the critical role that AVR plays in ensuring power quality across diverse renewable energy installations.',
    'common-avr-myths-debunked': 'The market for voltage regulation is full of misconceptions that lead to poor purchasing decisions. Some buyers overspend on unnecessary features, while others completely underestimate the protection their equipment needs. This guide separates fact from fiction by addressing the ten most common AVR myths. By the end, you will have a clear, evidence-based understanding of what AVR technology can and cannot do, helping you make an informed decision.',
    'digital-vs-relay-avr-comparison': 'When evaluating automatic voltage regulators, the choice between digital servo-controlled and relay-type technologies is fundamental. These two approaches to voltage regulation have distinctly different performance characteristics, cost profiles, and ideal applications. Many buyers make purchasing decisions based on price alone without understanding how technology affects real-world protection capability. This comprehensive comparison will help you understand which technology is truly right for your situation.',
    'avr-installation-mistakes-to-avoid': 'Proper AVR installation is critical to achieving the protection performance the manufacturer intended. Improper installation is one of the most common reasons AVR systems fail to deliver expected results or even cause damage to connected equipment. Even experienced electricians sometimes make critical mistakes when installing AVR systems due to the unique requirements of voltage regulation technology. This guide documents the most common installation errors and how to avoid them.',
    'whole-house-voltage-regulator-guide': 'Point-of-use voltage protectors only guard individual appliances, leaving the rest of your home unprotected. A whole-house voltage regulator, also called a whole-home AVR, provides centralized voltage protection for every outlet and hardwired appliance in the residence. This approach offers superior protection, simplified maintenance, and often better value for homeowners with multiple appliances that need protection. This guide covers everything you need to know about whole-house AVR systems.',
    'avr-understanding-response-time': 'Response time is one of the most misunderstood specifications in voltage regulation. It determines whether an AVR can protect against fast transients like lightning-induced surges or only slower rolling blackouts. Understanding response time is essential for matching AVR performance to your actual protection needs. This technical guide explains what response time means, how it is measured, and what response speeds are required for different equipment categories.',
    'surge-protector-vs-avr-differences': 'Consumer electronics retailers often position surge protectors and AVR as interchangeable protection solutions. This could not be further from the truth. While both devices aim to protect electronics, they address fundamentally different threats and are suited for different applications. Many buyers purchase a surge protector when they actually need an AVR, or vice versa. This guide explains the critical differences and helps you choose the right protection solution.',
    'default': `Understanding proper voltage regulation is essential for anyone operating electrical equipment in regions with unstable power grids. Automatic Voltage Regulators (AVR) provide critical protection by maintaining stable output voltage despite variations in input power supply. In many African and emerging markets, grid voltage can fluctuate dramatically — ranging from 160V to 280V when nominal voltage is 220-240V. This comprehensive guide covers everything you need to know about voltage regulation for your specific application.`
  }
  return content[slug] || content['default']
}

function getIntroBodyZH(slug) {
  const zhContent = {
    'three-phase-vs-single-phase-avr-guide': '电压不稳定是住宅和工业环境中设备故障最常见的原因之一。在非洲，电压波动经常超过260V，选择正确的自动稳压器（AVR）意味着持续运营与代价高昂的停机之间的区别。关键的第一个决定是您需要单相还是三相AVR系统。本指南详细介绍了如何为您的特定应用、负载要求和预算做出正确选择。',
    'avr-for-solar-power-systems': '太阳能发电系统正在非洲和新兴市场改变能源生产方式，但这也带来了独特的电压调节挑战。与稳定的电网电源不同，太阳能装置的直流到交流转换会产生可能危及敏感电子设备的电压波动。太阳能系统稳压器通过确保为您的家庭或设施供电的交流输出保持稳定来解决这些挑战。本指南涵盖为什么电压调节对太阳能装置至关重要以及如何为您的设置选择正确的稳压器。',
    'default': '在电网不稳定的地区，正确的电压调节对于任何操作电气设备的人都至关重要。自动电压稳压器（AVR）通过在输入电源波动时保持稳定的输出电压来提供关键保护。在许多非洲和新兴市场，电网电压可能会剧烈波动——当额定电压为220-240V时，范围从160V到280V。本综合指南涵盖您需要了解的关于电压调节的一切。'
  }
  return zhContent[slug] || zhContent['default']
}

function getCoreBody(slug) {
  return `The technical foundation of this topic centers on how voltage irregularities impact equipment performance and longevity. In practice, power quality issues in many African regions produce conditions that far exceed equipment design tolerances. Understanding these technical realities is the first step toward implementing effective protection.

Key technical facts include: Input voltage in many African markets regularly swings from 160V to 280V while equipment is designed for 220-240V ± 10%. Voltage sags (moments of low voltage) cause equipment to draw higher current, leading to overheating and premature failure. Voltage surges (moments of excessive voltage) can immediately destroy sensitive components. YOKE AVR systems respond to these challenges with regulation accuracy of ±2% to ±5% depending on model, and response times ranging from 10ms to 500ms.

The economic argument for AVR is compelling: a single incident of voltage-induced equipment failure can cost 5 to 20 times the annual cost of AVR protection. For industrial operations,每小时 downtime costs can easily exceed $1,000, making reliable voltage regulation one of the highest-return investments in facility infrastructure.`
}

function getCoreBodyZH(slug) {
  return `这个话题的技术基础集中在电压波动如何影响设备性能和寿命。在实践中，许多非洲地区的电力质量问题产生的条件远远超出设备设计容差。了解这些技术现实是实施有效保护的第一步。

关键的技术事实包括：在许多非洲市场，输入电压经常在160V至280V之间波动，而设备设计为220-240V ±10%。电压下降（低电压时刻）导致设备消耗更高电流，导致过热和过早故障。电压浪涌（过高电压时刻）可能立即损坏敏感组件。YOKE AVR系统以±2%至±5%的调节精度应对这些挑战（取决于型号），响应时间从10ms到500ms不等。

AVR的经济论证令人信服：一次电压引起的设备故障事件可能花费AVR保护年度成本的5到20倍。对于工业运营，每小时停机成本可能轻易超过1,000美元，使可靠的电压调节成为设施基础设施中最高回报的投资之一。`
}

